Because small local models do not reliably follow strict formatting instructions, the pipeline uses a best-effort parser rather than strict JSON parsing. After generation, the raw output is split line by line and any line containing a colon is matched against the nine allowed keys. If no valid key-value lines are found at all, the record is marked parse_ok = False and assigned parse_failed_local_model_output as an uncertainty flag. For fields with invalid values (e.g., an event_type not in the allowed six categories), the pipeline falls back to the safe default ("other") and logs a field-level flag such as invalid_event_type_from_model. All raw model outputs are retained in the local_model_raw_output column of extractions_raw.csv so that parse failures can be manually inspected. This approach trades strict validity for pipeline robustness, which is appropriate for a teaching demo but would need to be tightened in a production setting.}